VERSION:   4
COMMENT: epsilon-iron (Fe), hcp, P6_3/mmc - Miozzi et al. (2020) Minerals 10, 100, doi:10.3390/min10020100, table 1
COMMENT: Vinet fit at 300 K: V0=22.81 A3, K0=125(5) GPa, K0P=6.5(2), see Fe-hcp_BM3_Miozzi2020.jcpds for the 3rd order Birch-Murnaghan fit
COMMENT: WARNING: the EOS keyword is a pyFAI extension, other programs read K0/K0P as Birch-Murnaghan
COMMENT: Thermal model of the source: Mie-Gruneisen-Debye, thetaD=420 K (fixed), gamma0=1.11(1), q=0.3(3), reference 300 K, refined by the authors with the Birch-Murnaghan isotherm (MgO scale of Speziale et al. 2001)
COMMENT: ALPHAT, DALPHADT, DK0DT, DK0PDT fitted on this model applied to the Vinet isotherm (thermal pressure, as in Dioptas) between 30 and 140 GPa and 300 and 3400 K: pressure within 0.10 GPa, temperature within 15 K
COMMENT: epsilon-Fe is stable above about 16 GPa: V0 is an extrapolation
COMMENT: c/a=1.603 read on the inset of Fig. 1 of Dewaele et al. (2006) Phys. Rev. Lett. 97, 215504, doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.97.215504, at 20 GPa; c/a decreases to 1.597 at 150-200 GPa, not described by the EoS
COMMENT: Intensities calculated (Cu Ka, Cromer-Mann form factor of Cl used for Fe, no thermal factor)
